  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_FormatDuFichierD">Information file format</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_XsltAppliqueUneFeuille">xslt applies a transformation sheet to the canonical XML: this is what produces the exact structure an ECM expects, without shipping code.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_FeuilleDeTransformation">Transformation sheet</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_Parcourir">Browse</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_CheminSurLeServeur">Path on the SERVER. The button is only a typing aid and is relevant only when the interface runs on the server.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_ExtensionDuFichierProduit">Produced file extension (no dot)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_VideDonneXmlUne">Empty gives .xml. A sheet declaring method=text produces flat output: use txt, idx or csv depending on what the ECM expects.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S_Edit_MiseAuPointPasser">Development: set the format to xml, look at the output, write the sheet against it, then switch back to xslt. Both formats produce the same input XML.</s:String>
